WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.098
In March 1908 the Hope family crossed the

2
00:00:03.098 --> 00:00:05.896
Atlantic from England to Cleveland, Ohio.

3
00:00:06.246 --> 00:00:10.878
Among the seven sons was a four-year-old named Leslie Townes Hope.

4
00:00:11.228 --> 00:00:14.289
His father's first job there was carving stone for the Church of

5
00:00:14.289 --> 00:00:17.637
the Covenant, and he later worked on Cleveland's Guardians of Traffic.

6
00:00:17.987 --> 00:00:22.036
The boy went to the Fairmount schools and East High, sang in the Church

7
00:00:22.036 --> 00:00:26.143
of the Covenant choir, took dancing lessons, and boxed briefly under the

8
00:00:26.143 --> 00:00:30.363
name "Packy East" before losing in a novice championship and giving it up.

9
00:00:30.713 --> 00:00:34.969
Hope went into vaudeville in 1922, worked up through

10
00:00:34.969 --> 00:00:39.225
partner acts and Broadway revues, and in 1928 struck

11
00:00:39.225 --> 00:00:43.972
out as a solo comedian — changing his first name to "Bob."

12
00:00:44.322 --> 00:00:45.657
Hollywood made him a star.

13
00:00:46.007 --> 00:00:50.366
He took his radio show overseas in 1943, began his Christmas

14
00:00:50.366 --> 00:00:54.433
shows for the troops in 1948, and performed for American

15
00:00:54.433 --> 00:00:59.591
servicemen and women through the Korean War, Vietnam, and the Gulf War.

16
00:00:59.941 --> 00:01:03.596
In 1997 Congress made him the first civilian ever named

17
00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:07.185
an honorary veteran of the United States armed forces.

18
00:01:07.535 --> 00:01:09.904
Hope never took a citizenship oath of his own.

19
00:01:10.254 --> 00:01:12.629
Under the law of the time, a child became a

20
00:01:12.629 --> 00:01:15.501
citizen automatically when a parent was naturalised.

21
00:01:15.851 --> 00:01:17.593
As the record plainly states:

22
00:01:18.193 --> 00:01:21.164
“When his father was naturalized in December

23
00:01:21.164 --> 00:01:24.067
1920, Hope became a United States citizen.”

24
00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:25.782
He was seventeen.

25
00:01:26.132 --> 00:01:28.400
The boy who had crossed the Atlantic at four was

26
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.857
made an American by an act in which he took no part.

27
00:01:31.207 --> 00:01:35.317
This is the citation read out when he received his second Honorary Award:

28
00:01:35.917 --> 00:01:38.263
“To Bob Hope for unique and distinguished

29
00:01:38.263 --> 00:01:40.608
service to our industry and the Academy.”

30
00:01:41.208 --> 00:01:45.701
Is a citizen made by a ceremony, or by the life a person lives in a country?
